// The employment agreement between Harborlight Bakery and Nadia Okafor (employment.md).
Document "employment.md"

Fact party Identified by Harborlight, Nadia
Fact employer Identified by Harborlight
Fact employee Identified by Nadia
Fact usd Identified by Money(USD, 2)
Param salary : Money(USD, 2) = 600000
Param notice-period : Duration = 14
Param release-window : Duration = 21
Param non-solicit-period : Duration = 365

// 1. Employment: begins when both have signed; at will; fourteen days' notice
Fact signed Identified by party
Bool ended
Bool employed
  Holds when (Forall party: signed()) && Not(ended())
Act sign Actor party
  Holds when True
  Creates signed()

Bool dismissed
Bool dismissed-for-cause
Power dismiss Actor employer Recipient employee
  Holds when employed()
  Valid when employed()
  Creates ended(), dismissed(), dismissed-for-cause() When cause()

Bool notice-given
Act give-notice Actor employee Recipient employer
  Holds when employed()
  Creates notice-given()
Power leave Actor employee Recipient employer
  Holds when employed() && Held(notice-given()) For notice-period
  Valid when employed()
  Creates ended()

// 2. Pay: a month's salary five days after the month; an expense thirty days after submission
Fact month Identified by Int
Event month-ends Related to month
  Creates salary-due() When employed()
Duty salary-due Holder employer Claimant employee Related to month
  Due within 5
  Terminated by pay-salary
Act pay-salary Actor employer Recipient employee Related to month, usd
  Valid when usd == salary

Fact expense
Act submit-expense Actor employee Recipient employer Related to expense
  Holds when employed()
Duty reimbursement-due Holder employer Claimant employee Related to expense
  Due within 30
  Created by submit-expense
  Terminated by reimburse
Act reimburse Actor employer Recipient employee Related to expense

// 3. Cause, and severance on a release signed within twenty-one days
Bool warned
Act warn Actor employer Recipient employee
  Holds when employed()
  Creates warned()
Bool cause
Event theft Creates cause()
Event felony-conviction Creates cause()
Event neglect Creates cause() When warned()

Bool released
Bool released-in-time
Act sign-release Actor employee Recipient employer
  Holds when dismissed()
  Creates released(), released-in-time() When dismissed() && Not(Held(dismissed()) For release-window)
Bool severance-earned
  Default timely-release Holds when released-in-time()
  Exception for-cause Overrides timely-release Rejects when dismissed-for-cause()
Duty severance-due Holder employer Claimant employee
  Holds when severance-earned()
  Due within 10
  Terminated by pay-severance
Act pay-severance Actor employer Recipient employee Related to usd
  Valid when usd == salary * 2

// 4. After employment: confidentiality and the twelve months without soliciting
Fact secret
Fact consented Identified by secret
Act consent-to-disclosure Actor employer Recipient employee Related to secret
  Holds when True
  Creates consented()
Act disclose Actor employee Related to secret
  Holds when consented()

Fact staff
Act solicit Actor employee Related to staff
  Holds when Not(staff) || Not(ended()) || Held(ended()) For non-solicit-period

Clause 1.1 Approved "0dc1f1d5cc4d851355ea6cc8e7c343495ec524fc4f24d8531aee7eada76af10e"
  Definition "Harborlight Bakery, the employer, employs Nadia Okafor, the employee, as head baker."
  Norm " Employment begins when both have signed this agreement." => sign
Clause 1.2 Approved "0cfbffcf39e40a667f776aad1d8eea00a6d1d7a71ce249e88e7166b7b954bdc7"
  Norm "Employment is at will. Either party may end it at any time, with or without cause." => dismiss, leave
Clause 1.3 Approved "9d1c0b921eafc5f2bb3427732cefa5dc39973ae67120b186e60d329a4bffc9c9"
  Norm "The employee gives the employer fourteen days' notice before she leaves." => give-notice, leave
  Norm " Leaving without that notice is a breach of this agreement, but it still ends the employment." => leave
Clause 2.1 Approved "dc1415409b1bf9dd447f9825bad7d9ee861073bed0f5457b96e2a034dee5cb10"
  Definition "The salary is six thousand dollars a month."
  Norm " The employer pays each month's salary within five days after the month ends." => salary-due, pay-salary
Clause 2.2 Approved "001a1ff9ebe7b037272886f164d0e359da6bbfe391803339f099fc8f5902f37e"
  Norm "The employer reimburses a business expense within thirty days after the employee submits it." => submit-expense, reimbursement-due, reimburse
Clause 3.1 Approved "502a84026877abd9b0d3d102ad490f2f03bedb8ade744b846a2b61dd7ad21e78"
  Norm "The employer has cause to terminate when the employee has stolen from the employer, has been convicted of a felony, or has neglected her duties after a written warning." => warn, dismiss
Clause 3.2 Approved "f49c9d6d14016ad576f1aad77d0ab542884e7026c74f97405706ba0616434ef1"
  Norm "If the employer terminates the employment and the employee signs a release of claims within twenty-one days after the termination, the employer pays her severance of two months' salary within ten days after she signs." => sign-release, severance-due, pay-severance
  Norm " A release signed later than that earns no severance." => sign-release
Clause 3.3 Approved "f405e0e4b1322771aaaed972d7603b4b5c513b169366ce46e268994c091a8c9a"
  Norm "A termination for cause carries no severance." => dismiss, severance-due
Clause 4.1 Approved "acd098078b143d005cebb15a9ed0fa7f6415f4c929fa3444f8844f26154e3c41"
  Norm "The employee discloses the employer's confidential information only with the employer's written consent." => disclose, consent-to-disclosure
  Norm " This clause continues to bind her after the employment ends." => disclose
Clause 4.2 Approved "dd38532ef50e1255cad4d88ed149ce4145b0ebedbe5b4e843acbd5fdd1322653"
  Norm "For twelve months after the employment ends, the employee does not solicit any member of the employer's staff to leave the employer." => solicit
Clause 4.3 Approved "39451e37d7ebd00c1887e4cf5e35ff30f78455bd08b8564eabdec1e8cfaa95a4"
  Norm "Salary and expenses that fell due before the employment ended remain payable after it." => salary-due, reimbursement-due
.
